# Platform Rules

crossroot supports **Windows (Git Bash)**, **macOS**, and **Linux** as first-class platforms.

## Shell Baseline

- All scripts use `#!/usr/bin/env bash` and `set -euo pipefail`.
- **Git Bash is required on Windows.** Do not use PowerShell for repo operations.
- `uv`, `nox`, and all tools are invoked identically on all platforms.
- Use forward slashes in paths inside scripts and configs.

## Windows (Git Bash)

- Install [Git for Windows](https://git-scm.com/downloads) to get Git Bash.
- Run `croot` and all `.sh` scripts in Git Bash.
- Add `scripts/` to `PATH` in `~/.bash_profile` (not `~/.bashrc`):
  ```bash
  export PATH="$PATH:/d/src/{{ repo_slug }}/scripts"
  ```
- Avoid paths with spaces where possible; if unavoidable, quote them: `"path with spaces"`.
- `uv` on Windows installs to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\uv\bin`; ensure that's in your system `PATH`.

## macOS

- Install uv: `curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh`
- Ensure `~/.local/bin` is in `PATH` (the uv installer advises this).
- `croot` works in bash and zsh.

## Linux

- Install uv via the same installer: `curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh`
- `croot` works in bash and zsh.

## CI Matrix

CI runs on `ubuntu-latest`, `macos-latest`, and `windows-latest` to catch platform-specific issues early. Always run `croot check` locally before pushing.

## Cross-Platform Dos and Don'ts

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| `#!/usr/bin/env bash` | `#!/bin/bash` (not available on all systems) |
| `uv run python` | `python3` or `python` directly (venv may not be active) |
| Forward slashes in paths | Backslashes in scripts |
| `$()` for command substitution | Backtick substitution |
| `[[ ... ]]` for conditionals | `[ ... ]` for complex expressions |
